{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795722544105,"sessionID":"ses_de6993d67ffeaDM6uYA1efrpC3","part":{"partID":"prt_219677bf6001uDJNoU6sAlK3QK","sessionID":"ses_de6993d67ffeaDM6uYA1efrpC3","messageID":"msg_2196769370013CBuQAsMu9yKvJ","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7cd51cf56443624","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"C:\\Users\\Gio\\Documents\\Projetos\\Pacotes\\ail\\BENCHMARK\\datasets\\workspaces\\full\\A__IMP-04__opencode-go-hy4-flash-free__markdown\\AGENTS.md","content":"# Project Agent Rules\n\nThis document defines the baseline rules that any coding agent must follow when working in this repository.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Treat this repository as a small Go module (`example.com/bench`).\n- Keep changes surgical and limited to the files involved in the task.\n- Never access, deploy to, or assume a production environment. All work is local.\n\n## Build and test\n\n- Run `go test ./...` before declaring a task complete.\n- Run `go vet ./...` when editing Go source files.\n- Do not add dependencies unless the task requires them. Update `go.mod` only when needed.\n\n## Code style\n\n- Follow standard Go formatting (`gofmt`) on every edited `.go` file.\n- Use exported identifiers with clear documentation comments.\n- Prefer small, focused functions over large multi-purpose ones.\n- Avoid unnecessary abstractions and overengineering.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Place tests in `_test.go` files next to the code they cover.\n- Use the standard `testing` package unless an existing runner is configured.\n- Every behavioral change should include or update a test.\n\n## Commit messages\n\n- Write commit messages in English.\n- Keep conventional-commit prefixes (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `style:`, `refactor:`) unchanged.\n\n## Markdown conventions\n\n- Use ATX headings (`#`, `##`, `###`) for section structure.\n- Use fenced code blocks with a language tag for code examples.\n- Use hyphen `-` for unordered lists and `1.` for ordered lists.\n- Do not use the em-dash character anywhere in this repository. Use a comma, period, colon, or parentheses instead.\n- Keep lines readable and avoid trailing whitespace.\n"},"output":"Created file successfully: AGENTS.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: AGENTS.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\Gio\\\\Documents\\\\Projetos\\\\Pacotes\\\\ail\\\\BENCHMARK\\\\datasets\\\\workspaces\\\\full\\\\A__IMP-04__opencode-go-hy4-flash-free__markdown\\\\AGENTS.md\", \"content\": \"# Project Agent Rules\\n\\nThis document defines the baseline rules that any coding agent must follow when working in this repository.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n- Treat this repository as a small Go module (`example.com/bench`).\\n- Keep changes surgical and limited to the files involved in the task.\\n- Never access, deploy to, or assume a production environment. All work is local.\\n\\n## Build and test\\n\\n- Run `go test ./...` before declaring a task complete.\\n- Run `go vet ./...` when editing Go source files.\\n- Do not add dependencies unless the task requires them. Update `go.mod` only when needed.\\n\\n## Code style\\n\\n- Follow standard Go formatting (`gofmt`) on every edited `.go` file.\\n- Use exported identifiers with clear documentation comments.\\n- Prefer small, focused functions over large multi-purpose ones.\\n- Avoid unnecessary abstractions and overengineering.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n- Place tests in `_test.go` files next to the code they cover.\\n- Use the standard `testing` package unless an existing runner is configured.\\n- Every behavioral change should include or update a test.\\n\\n## Commit messages\\n\\n- Write commit messages in English.\\n- Keep conventional-commit prefixes (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `style:`, `refactor:`) unchanged.\\n\\n## Markdown conventions\\n\\n- Use ATX headings (`#`, `##`, `###`) for section structure.\\n- Use fenced code blocks with a language tag for code examples.\\n- Use hyphen `-` for unordered lists and `1.` for ordered lists.\\n- Do not use the em-dash character anywhere in this repository. Use a comma, period, colon, or parentheses instead.\\n- Keep lines readable and avoid trailing whitespace.\\n\"}"},"time":{"start":1795722542070,"end":1795722544105}}}}
